    <dcterms:title>Poor Miss Finch</dcterms:title>
    <dcterms:description>Wikipedia page about this book: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poor_Miss_Finch</dcterms:description>
    <pgterms:marc508>Produced by James Rusk</pgterms:marc508>
    <pgterms:marc520>"Poor Miss Finch" by Wilkie Collins is a novel published in 1872. It follows Lucilla Finch, a young blind woman who falls in love with Oscar Dubourg, her reclusive neighbor. When Oscar's medical treatment leaves him permanently disfigured with blue-grey skin—triggering Lucilla's phobia of dark colors—his charming twin brother Nugent arrives from America. As Lucilla undergoes surgery that may restore her sight, a dangerous deception unfolds involving mistaken identity, manipulation, and a race against time to prevent a disastrous marriage. (This is an automatically generated summary.)</pgterms:marc520>
    <pgterms:marc908>Reading ease score: 73.9 (7th grade). Fairly easy to read.</pgterms:marc908>
